Comedian\'92s Log \'96 Week 1 on Asteroid Nemo\
Location: Somewhere between Mars and Jupiter\
Population: Me, a couple of rocks I\'92ve named, and a vending machine that speaks only in passive-aggressive beeps.\
Mission: Survive. Or at least make sarcastic commentary until rescue arrives.\
Day 1 \'96 Arrival\
Woke up from cryosleep to the sound of the onboard AI saying, \'93You may experience slight disorientation.\'94\
Slight disorientation? I stepped out of the pod and immediately thought the ceiling was the floor. Walked into what I thought was a door. It was the bathroom mirror. I apologized to my own reflection.\
Discovered my assignment: study asteroid Nemo\'92s mineral content. My reaction: \'93Cool, so I\'92m space\'92s least glamorous geologist.\'94\
Tried to plant my Earth flag in the ground. Forgot there\'92s no atmosphere, so it fell over like a drunk flamingo.\
Day 2 \'96 Naming Rocks\
There\'92s not much to do here, so I started naming the local boulders.\
Big one near the habitat: \'93Rocky Balboa\'94\
Smaller one with a chip on the side: \'93Bitey\'94\
One that keeps rolling into my path every morning: \'93Gary,\'94 because he looks like he\'92s judging me.\
Tried to do my stand-up routine for them. Rocky was stone-faced (literally), Gary rolled away mid-joke, and Bitey just\'85 sat there.\
Made a mental note: even imaginary hecklers are exhausting.\
Day 3 \'96 First Grocery Inventory\
Discovered my food supply is mostly freeze-dried stuff:\
Pasta that tastes like cardboard\
Cardboard that tastes like pasta\
A suspiciously large stash of \'93Space Kale,\'94 which is neither spacey nor kale-y.\
Decided to spice things up by combining two meals into one. Result: \'93Soy-flavored oatmeal surprise.\'94 Surprise was that my digestive system called me an idiot for hours afterward.\
Day 4 \'96 Exercise Day\
The AI suggested I \'93stay active to maintain muscle mass.\'94\
Tried jogging in the habitat. Ended up bouncing off a wall into my storage shelf, which is now dented in the shape of my head.\
The AI laughed. I didn\'92t even know it could laugh. I think I\'92ve unlocked a new level of humiliation.\
Day 5 \'96 Found My Purpose\'85 Sort Of\
Discovered Nemo\'92s surface sparkles at sunrise. Probably some mineral deposit, but I\'92ve decided it\'92s glitter dust from a cosmic party I wasn\'92t invited to.\
Thought about doing a \'93mineral review\'94 vlog. First episode: \'93Quartz \'97 nature\'92s way of saying \'91I\'92m shiny, but you can\'92t eat me.\'92\'94\
Audience: still just Rocky, Gary, and Bitey. Engagement: 0 likes, 0 shares.\
Day 6 \'96 Mental Games\
Invented a game: \'93Will this space snack taste worse than it looks?\'94 Spoiler: yes.\
Wrote an open letter to whoever designed the habitat\'92s furniture: \'93Why is the chair shaped like a hexagon? My body is not shaped like a hexagon.\'94\
Started giving myself stage names for each room.\
Kitchen: \'93Chef L\'92Depression\'94\
Lab: \'93Dr. Who-Cares\'94\
Sleeping quarters: \'93The Nap Trap\'94\
Day 7 \'96 One Week Anniversary\
Threw myself a party for surviving a week. Guest list: me, my rocks, and the vending machine.\
Made a cake out of compressed protein bars. It tasted like regret and chalk.\
Did a comedy set for my \'93guests.\'94 Punchline of the night: \'93You know you\'92re lonely when you start arguing with the oxygen filter \'97 and lose.\'94\
Realized I might be losing my mind\'85 but at least I\'92ll have killer material for when I get back to Earth. If I ever get back to Earth.\
