\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \'93Dust, Silence, and a Rock Named Gary\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b0\fs24 \cf0 (A Long-Form Nemo Epic)
\f0\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 I came to Nemo by accident,\uc0\u8232 not by choice,\u8232 not by plan,\u8232 but by the kind of cosmic joke\u8232 that makes the universe lean in and whisper,\u8232 
\f2\i \'93Let\'92s see how you handle this one.\'94
\f0\i0 \
There was no crowd to greet me,\uc0\u8232 no velvet curtain to pull back,\u8232 only dust \'97\u8232 dust that clung to boots, to gloves, to thoughts,\u8232 and the unblinking stars\u8232 that hung above like\u8232 distant theater lights I could never reach.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Day 1:
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 I named the rock Gary.\u8232 It was either that\u8232 or name myself,\u8232 and I thought it best\u8232 to keep some distance.\
Gary was patient.\uc0\u8232 Gary was still.\u8232 Gary never laughed at my jokes \'97\u8232 but Gary never left.\u8232 And in those early hours,\u8232 that counted for more than applause.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 I learned the weather quickly:\uc0\u8232 always dusty,\u8232 always still.\u8232 A forecast you could trust,\u8232 like a bad running gag\u8232 that somehow grows on you.\
I made rituals \'97\uc0\u8232 fake news broadcasts,\u8232 pretend parades,\u8232 cooking shows with no real ingredients.\u8232 A comedian needs an audience,\u8232 and when you don\'92t have one,\u8232 you become both performer and crowd.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 I spoke to the AI often,\uc0\u8232 though its voice\u8232 was the kind that feels like\u8232 it\'92s reading your eulogy\u8232 before you\'92re dead.\u8232 It tried to comfort me with data.\u8232 I tried to comfort it with punchlines.\u8232 We both failed and succeeded in turns.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 I invented a presidency for Gary.\uc0\u8232 I wrote campaign speeches.\u8232 I staged debates.\u8232 I declared him re-elected in a landslide\u8232 of one vote to zero.\u8232 It was the cleanest political process\u8232 in human history.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The food \'97\uc0\u8232 I could write a hundred stanzas\u8232 on the food.\u8232 Protein bars that tasted like\u8232 compressed cardboard memories.\u8232 Kale that came in packets\u8232 so untrustworthy\u8232 you half-expected them to hiss.\u8232 And yet, each meal was a kind of hope:\u8232 hope that tomorrow\u8232 I\'92d find a better way to eat it,\u8232 hope that someday\u8232 I\'92d eat something green that didn\'92t crunch like glass.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Nights on Nemo were\uc0\u8232 endless matinees of the same show:\u8232 the dark,\u8232 the stars,\u8232 the silence that wasn\'92t silence at all\u8232 but a low hum of my own blood\u8232 reminding me I was still here.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 The days blurred.
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 Sometimes I counted them.\u8232 Sometimes I didn\'92t.\u8232 Sometimes I measured time by\u8232 the number of dust motes I watched drift past the porthole.\u8232 Sometimes I measured it by\u8232 the new ways I could think about Gary.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 And then,\uc0\u8232 there was the letter.\
Clara \'97\uc0\u8232 I don\'92t know if it reached you.\u8232 I don\'92t know if you read it once or twice,\u8232 or if you laughed,\u8232 or if you sighed.\u8232 But I know I needed to write it.\u8232 Not because I thought you\'92d come,\u8232 but because I needed to say\u8232 I was still me.\u8232 That Nemo hadn\'92t taken that.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 I built monuments of rocks that floated away.\uc0\u8232 I sang to dust that never answered.\u8232 I laughed at my own jokes\u8232 and sometimes hated myself for it.\u8232 I stopped caring about haircuts,\u8232 or days of the week,\u8232 or how loud my voice sounded in my helmet.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 When they told me rescue was coming,\uc0\u8232 I didn\'92t believe it.\u8232 Hope feels strange\u8232 when you\'92ve been living in a place\u8232 that doesn\'92t trade in it.\u8232 And when I finally saw the rescue ship \'97\u8232 a pinprick,\u8232 then a promise,\u8232 then a home \'97\u8232 I realized Nemo was about to become\u8232 someone else\'92s problem,\u8232 and my problem was about to become\u8232 how to leave it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The last week,\uc0\u8232 I did everything for the last time:\u8232 last weather report (dusty),\u8232 last parade for Gary (victorious),\u8232 last protein bar dinner (tragic).\u8232 I said goodbye to a rock,\u8232 and I meant it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Boarding the rescue ship felt like\uc0\u8232 stepping back into a forgotten skin.\u8232 Voices.\u8232 Faces.\u8232 Food that tasted like intention.\u8232 And yet,\u8232 part of me kept looking out the porthole,\u8232 watching Nemo shrink\u8232 until it was just a speck,\u8232 until it was nothing,\u8232 until it was everything again.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Now I sit here,\uc0\u8232 writing in a room that hums with machinery,\u8232 surrounded by people who ask me\u8232 how it was.\u8232 I tell them it was dusty.\u8232 I tell them it was lonely.\u8232 I tell them it was absurd.\u8232 But I don\'92t tell them that sometimes,\u8232 I miss it \'97\u8232 because missing a place like Nemo\u8232 sounds insane\u8232 until you\'92ve lived there.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 So here\'92s to Nemo:\uc0\u8232 to dust and silence,\u8232 to laughter with no echo,\u8232 to rocks with names,\u8232 to meals you eat only because you have to,\u8232 to the quiet kind of survival\u8232 that doesn\'92t look brave\u8232 until you\'92re far enough away to see it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 And here\'92s to Gary,\uc0\u8232 the only audience member\u8232 who never walked out on me.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

