\f1\b \cf0 Subject:
\f0\b0  
\f2\i Re: An Invitation to Make History (and Possibly Regret Several Creative Choices)
\f0\i0 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\b From:
\f0\b0  [Comedian\'92s Name]\uc0\u8232 
\f1\b To:
\f0\b0  Samantha L. Gold, Senior VP of Creative Development, StarHorizon Studios\uc0\u8232 
\f1\b Date:
\f0\b0  [Week 24, Day 165]\
Dear Samantha,\
First of all, thank you for your letter. I\'92ve read it twice \'97 once out of curiosity, and once to make sure it wasn\'92t some elaborate prank pulled by one of my friends who still thinks I hallucinated Gary. Judging by the studio letterhead, the corporate enthusiasm, and the fact that you actually budgeted for a \'93personal assistant for Gary,\'94 I\'92m going to assume this is real.\
Let me start by saying: I am 
\f2\i flattered
\f0\i0 . I did not expect my months of talking to a rock, rationing dehydrated curry, and singing to myself in the dead silence of space to be considered marketable entertainment. (Well, I suspected my mum might watch it, but I thought she\'92d have to bring her own popcorn.)\
That said \'97 before I sign on to what sounds like a potentially spectacular adventure (or a catastrophic misunderstanding between art and commerce), I\'92d like to address a few key points from your proposal.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 1. The Title
\f0\b0 \
I have\'85 feelings. Let\'92s unpack them:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls144\ilvl0
\f2\i \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Alone on Nemo
\f0\i0  \'97 Yes, technically accurate. However, it makes it sound like I was doing interpretive dance on a clownfish.\
\ls144\ilvl0
\f2\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Laughing in the Void
\f0\i0  \'97 This feels closer. It captures the absurdity of trying to make jokes when the nearest audience is 150 million kilometers away and already bored.\
\ls144\ilvl0
\f2\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Gary & Me
\f0\i0  \'97 I can\'92t deny the charm, but I fear it implies a rom-com. There are only so many ways to clarify to strangers that I did not, in fact, marry my rock.\
\ls144\ilvl0
\f2\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Survivor: Space
\f0\i0  \'97 You are right; this will get us sued by reality television lawyers before opening night.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 My own working title has always been 
\f2\i A Long Conversation with Silence
\f0\i0 . Not very poster-friendly, I know, but it\'92s the truth. Still, I am willing to workshop something that captures both the existential dread and the occasional fart joke.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 2. Tone & Genre
\f0\b0 \
You\'92ve pitched a dramedy. That\'92s fair. My life out there was exactly that: one part \'93man faces the abyss,\'94 one part \'93man accidentally glues sock to air filter.\'94\
I do, however, have concerns about leaning too hard into the comedy without honoring the quieter, darker moments. There were days when the silence didn\'92t feel like a peaceful hush but like a heavy blanket pressing down. There were nights when I wasn\'92t sure I\'92d see Earth again, and I\'92d just stare at the tiny blue dot out the viewport. Those moments are important. If we erase them in favor of non-stop banter, we risk turning this into 
\f2\i The Hangover in Space
\f0\i0 . (And trust me, no one wants to wake up with a hangover 
\f2\i and
\f0\i0  zero gravity.)\
Comedy without truth is just noise. The laughs on Nemo came from tension breaking, not from ignoring it. If we can capture that balance, then yes \'97 let\'92s make people laugh through their tears.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 3. Casting
\f0\b0 \
I appreciate that you\'92re offering me the chance to play myself. However, I must warn you: I am not a trained actor. The last time I tried to deliver scripted lines was in my secondary school production of 
\f2\i Macbeth
\f0\i0 , where I played \'93Third Murderer\'94 and forgot to enter the stage entirely.\
If you insist on casting a professional, Paul Rudd seems like a safe bet \'97 though he is far too handsome to accurately portray the \'93post-oxygen-ration\'94 version of me. Adam Driver has the intense stare down, but I fear he\'92d make Gary seem like a metaphor for my father. Oscar Isaac would be\'85 well, Oscar Isaac. No complaints there.\
As for Gary \'97 please don\'92t animate him. Part of Gary\'92s charm was that he did not move, speak, or have facial expressions. All his \'93character\'94 came from my projection. If you give him a CGI smirk, you\'92ve missed the point entirely.\
That said, I am not opposed to a stunt Gary for particularly dangerous scenes. (I imagine the real Gary would appreciate the union rules.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 4. Supporting Characters
\f0\b0 \
A \'93rival astronaut\'94 sounds fun, but in reality, there was no competition. The only rival I had was entropy. And maybe the malfunctioning coffee recycler. I don\'92t want to invent drama that undermines the actual challenges.\
If we need human connections, I\'92d rather highlight the mission control team, the random engineers who kept me alive from across the void, and the occasional snippets of Earth broadcasts I picked up. One of my favorite memories was hearing a cricket match commentary halfway through a comms blackout. That sort of serendipity says more about isolation than any made-up antagonist could.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 5. Creative Freedom
\f0\b0 \
You said: 
\f2\i \'93You\'92ll have final say on the jokes. We\'92ll have final say on\'85 everything else. (Kidding! Mostly.)\'94
\f0\i0 \
I read that \'93mostly\'94 louder than the rest of the sentence. I understand how studio filmmaking works. I also understand that if you want me to be genuinely invested, I need a real seat at the creative table, not a folding chair at the kiddie end.\
I am not precious about every detail \'97 if you want to change my jumpsuit color for better lighting, fine. But if you suggest adding an action sequence where I fight space pirates, I\'92m going to need you to explain where those pirates were hiding.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 6. Budget
\f0\b0 \
Eight figures sounds\'85 dizzying. My whole Nemo mission cost less than that. If you want authenticity, you don\'92t need Iceland for asteroid shots \'97 you need a disused quarry, a few lights, and a willingness to get dust in your shoes.\
That said, I am not against some spectacle. Just remember: the real story\'92s power comes from restraint, not fireworks. If people leave saying, \'93Wow, I felt like I was there,\'94 we\'92ve done our job. If they leave saying, \'93Wow, that explosion was sick,\'94 we\'92ve made a different film entirely.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 7. Merchandising
\f0\b0 \
Gary plush toys \'97 fine. I will sign those. Branded asteroid survival kits for kids \'97 borderline. If they include actual freeze-dried food, please, for the love of taste buds, make sure it\'92s edible.\
Space helmets with my catchphrases\'85 I can already hear the arguments in the toy aisle. \'93Mum, I want the helmet that says \'91Don\'92t talk to me, I\'92m talking to my rock.\'92\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 8. Timeline
\f0\b0 \
This is fast. Very fast. My worry is that in the rush to hit a summer festival, we\'92ll sand down the rough edges that made the story worth telling. I\'92d rather take six more months and make something timeless than rush out a film that feels like a cash grab.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 My Counterproposal
\f0\b0 \
I\'92m willing to co-write and consult, but I need:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls145\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Real creative input, beyond just punching up the jokes.\
\ls145\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A commitment to authenticity over spectacle.\
\ls145\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Respect for Gary\'92s\'85 dignity. He is, after all, my co-star.\
\ls145\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Freedom to veto any plot points that involve alien invasions, surprise evil twins, or musical numbers (unless I\'92m the one suggesting them).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 In exchange, I will:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls146\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Provide detailed accounts of my time on Nemo, including the unpublished logs.\
\ls146\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Help shape the tone so it lands between truth and entertainment.\
\ls146\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Participate in press, provided no one tries to make me wear a spacesuit at every interview.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Why This Matters to Me
\f0\b0 \
Samantha, I know in your world this is \'93content.\'94 But in mine, it was months of my life. It was the sound of my own breathing in a tin can surrounded by nothing. It was the weight of silence pressing in until I broke it with a joke. It was real fear, real boredom, real moments of grace.\
If we make this film, I want it to honor not just my survival, but the survival of anyone who\'92s ever been stuck in a place they didn\'92t choose, trying to make it to tomorrow with whatever scraps of hope they could find.\
Yes, we can make it funny. Yes, we can make it big. But we must make it 
\f2\i true
\f0\i0 . Otherwise, we\'92re just playing dress-up in space.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Final Thought
\f0\b0 \
I\'92m intrigued. I\'92m cautious. And I\'92m open to meeting in person to talk this through \'97 provided the coffee is better than what I had on Nemo. (That\'92s not a high bar, but I feel compelled to mention it.)\
Yours in low gravity,\
Comedian\
