\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 VI. The Nemo Psychological Aftermath\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 I didn\'92t expect coming home to be harder than staying on Nemo. But Earth is loud. Too many smells. Too many people trying to hand me things. Fame is stranger than silence. On Nemo, my only audience was a rock. Now it\'92s millions of people, each with their own idea of what my story \'93really means.\'94\
I\'92ll tell you what it means:\uc0\u8232 It means you can be the loneliest man alive and still laugh at your own dumb jokes.\u8232 It means even a rock can be a friend if you treat it right.\u8232 It means Hollywood better not screw this up, because the truth is already enough.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
